  "query_preview": "..\n\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Mild weather pattern continues under southwest flow into next\n   week.\n\n-  Periods of valley fog and low clouds (stratus), especially in\n   western Montana.\n\n-  A weather system will bring showers, light rain or snow, and\n   high-elevation snow on Sunday.\n\nHigh pressure is re-establishing itself over the Northern Rockies today,\nresulting in daily fog and stratus developing each morning through\nSaturday. Patchy areas, especially along bodies of water, can expect dense\nfog. Once the fog and low clouds settle in, they will linger for several\nhours and be slow to clear. If widespread low clouds persist, afternoon\ntemperatures will struggle to reach forecast highs.\n\nThe next weather system will track through the Northwest, moving along the\nCanadian border on Sunday. A trough will break down the ridge of high\npressure, bringing showers and high-elevation snow (above 5,500 feet) along\nthe Idaho/Montana border and in northwest Montana. Winds will also\nincrease, with valley gusts up to 25 mph and higher elevations experiencing\ngusts of 30 to 40 mph. These winds will also help break up the valley\ninversions that develop on Friday and Saturday.\n\nLong-range forecast models suggest high pressure will rebuild to start next\nweek. This pattern will once again favor areas of valley fog and\nstratus.",
